    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0569" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW (Peace)/7–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-05T08:00:00+01:00">July 5, 1947—8 a.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>753. Despite what Bebler<anchor n="1" xml:id="d336-f1"/> told me Tuesday (Embtel
                    734 July 1 repeated Rome 72<anchor n="2" xml:id="d336-f2"/>) I understand
                    Italian Treaty has not yet been ratified by Presidium. Reason given by Foreign
                    Office is that ratification should first be completed for Bulgarian and
                    Hungarian treaties since these are now considered friendly nations.</p>
                <p>Sent Department as 753, repeated Rome 78.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d336-f1" n="1" xml:id="d336-f1-content">
                <p>Aleš Bebler, Yugoslav Assistant Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f2" n="2" xml:id="d336-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it Cabot reported that: “Bebler informed me today that Yugos
                    would ratify Italian treaty this afternoon.” (740.0011 EW (Peace)/6–147)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
